course: dictionary
lesson: 9254
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The word sound is a good example. Read the words around it to find out which meaning is meant. «Sound travels through air, water and solids, but not through empty space.» Here sound means something you can hear.
explain: «That sounds like praise.» Here sounds is a verb and means seems, when heard or read. The clue is praise: it is a kind of comment, so the sentence is about how something seems. Try your meaning in the sentence to check it.
explain: Sound can also be an adjective, meaning healthy, strong or sensible, as in «sound advice». Look at the words next to it. A sound plan or sound advice is a good one that you can trust, not a noise.
fact: Sound can be a noun, a verb or an adjective.
fact: As a noun, sound means anything you can hear, such as the sound of rain.
fact: As a verb, sound can mean to make a signal, as in «Sound the alarm», or to seem, as in «That sounds fun».
fact: As an adjective, sound means healthy, strong or sensible, as in «safe and sound».
fact: Sound is made by vibrations that travel through air, water and solids to our ears, but it cannot travel through empty space.
exercise: «Sound travels through air, water and solids, but not through empty space.» In this sentence, what is sound? | A narrow stretch of sea | Healthy and strong | *Something you can hear | To make a signal
exercise: «That sounds like praise.» What does sounds mean here? | Makes a loud noise | Is a narrow stretch of sea | *Seems, when heard or read | Is healthy
exercise: Mum says, «Your advice is sound.» What does sound mean? | *Sensible and good | A very loud noise | To make a signal | A narrow stretch of sea
test: In «Sound the alarm!», what does sound mean? | *To make a signal | Healthy and strong | Something you can hear | Seems, when heard or read
test: «Safe and sound» means | Lost at sea | Loud and noisy | *Safe and unharmed | Very tired and sleepy
exam: In «The bridge is sound», what does sound mean? | Something you hear | To make a noise | *Strong and safe | Seems, when heard or read
